---
import { linkInstagramMentions } from "../../utils/instagramMentions"

const inspiration = linkInstagramMentions("Inspired by Anu (@karnpapon) and recent redacted documents.")
---

<div class="mt-4 max-w-3xl">
  <p class="mb-6 text-sm opacity-80">What cannot be said becomes the beat</p>

  <p class="mb-4">
    I made a Chrome extension called Self-censored Step Sequencer. It turns redacted text into rhythm.
    In the age of blacked-out documents, what you cannot say becomes the beat. This extension turns
    silence into music.
  </p>

  <p class="mb-4 text-sm opacity-80" set:html={inspiration}></p>

  <figure class="my-8">
    <img
      src="/images/self-censored-step-sequencer-chrome-extension.jpg"
      alt="Self-censored Step Sequencer Chrome extension screenshot"
      class="w-full"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </figure>

  <h2 class="font-light text-xl mb-3 mt-8">Tool-making context</h2>

  <p class="mb-4">
    I started from what TouchDesigner was not good at for this use case, then shifted the problem into
    a browser extension workflow. The sequencing direction came after seeing a friend's piece that used
    RegEx as the sequencing mechanism.
  </p>

  <h2 class="font-light text-xl mb-3 mt-8">How it works</h2>

  <p class="mb-4">
    Open a webpage and click the extension, select a text area, then highlight words or redacted
    fragments. Press play and set BPM — the sequencer steps word-by-word, and redacted words glow while
    triggering drum hits.
  </p>

  <h2 class="font-light text-xl mb-3 mt-8">Modes</h2>

  <ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-4">
    <li class="mt-2">
      <strong>Local engine (WebSocket + OSC)</strong> — WebSocket events bridged to OSC via
      <code class="text-sm">bridge.js</code> in the repo; best for live and custom routing.
    </li>
    <li class="mt-2">
      <strong>Browser playback presets</strong> — Kick, snare, hi-hat, open hat, laser; fast setup with
      no local engine required.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="font-light text-xl mb-3 mt-8">Layouts</h2>

  <p class="mb-4">
    Overlay and sidebar presentation arrangements. Overlay is used in the first and second modes;
    sidebar is used in the third.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-neutral-800 text-sm space-y-2">
    <p>
      <strong>Chrome Web Store:</strong>
      <a
        href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/self-censored-step-sequen/ebechoeekjbgipgabcafpbfhenhpfaei"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="underline"
        style="color: var(--text-muted);"
      >
        Self-censored Step Sequencer
      </a>
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Repository:</strong>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/dodadoa/redacted-dm"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="underline"
        style="color: var(--text-muted);"
      >
        github.com/dodadoa/redacted-dm
      </a>
    </p>
    <p class="opacity-80">
      If you encounter bugs, please report them or send a pull request. Thank you.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
